{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A7]In the [Dm]fifth month of that year
The prop[Gm7]het Hananiah stood
In the house of the [Bb]LORD
Before the priests and crowd
He [A7sus4]spoke in the [A7]name [Dm]of God
That Babylon's rule [Gm7]would cease
And vessels would re[Bb]turn
From the distant Baby[Asus4]lon
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He would bring back [A]Jeconiah
[Dm]And all the exiles home
With[Gm]in two years he said
The [Bb]yoke would be undone
Jeremi[Asus4]ah replied Amen
[A]May the LORD [Dm]do so
But listen to [Gm]my word
To you and to [Bb]the crowd
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Prophets long before your [Asus4]time
Spoke of war and [A]plague
But he [Dm]who prophesies peace
Must see [Gm]it come to pass
Then Hana[C]niah took the yoke
From the [F]prophet's neck
He [A]broke it in [Dm]pieces
Before the eyes [Gm]of all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
He [Bb]declared to the people
[A]That God had spoken
That within two years
[Dm]He'd break the yoke off
[Gm]Jeremiah went his way
[Bb]But the word came to him
You broke yokes [Asus4]of wood
[A]Yet you [Dm]made yokes of iron
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
The LORD [Gm]of hosts has put
An [Bb]iron yoke on them
To [Asus4]serve Nebuchadnez[A]zar
And [Dm]serve him they will
The wild [Gm]animals given
To [C]the king of Babylon
You [F]have made them [A]trust
In [Dm]a great and heavy lie [Gm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[C]Hananiah died in the sev[F]enth month
[A]In that very same [Dm][Am/C]year
{end_of_verse}

